1. DEFINITIONS

"Project Owner" means Nicholas Thomas, operating as BlackhatShiftey, or a
successor that owns the applicable copyrights.

"Private Repository" means the non-public SEAM development repository,
including its source code, specifications, schemas, documentation, tests,
benchmarks, fixtures, designs, research, build and release tooling, history,
and other materials.

"Reserved Materials" means all material in the Private Repository that is not
expressly identified in writing by the Project Owner as carrying another
license.

"MIRL Reserved Materials" means the copyrighted expression and non-public
implementation materials relating to MIRL, including:

- the MIRL specifications, explanatory text, diagrams, examples, record
  definitions, schemas, grammars, serializations, field selections, and
  authored arrangements or compilations;
- source code and documentation for MIRL records, compilation, decompilation,
  extraction, grounding, normalization, reconciliation, storage, indexing,
  retrieval, graph projection, vectorization, and provenance;
- PACK, symbol-table, improvement-loop, compression, readable-compression,
  lossless, LX, RC, and related codec implementations or documentation;
- SDK, CLI, API, MCP, dashboard, benchmark, test, fixture, and integration
  material that implements, exposes, evaluates, or is derived from the
  non-public MIRL implementation; and
- non-public modifications, extensions, ports, translations, or derivative
  works of any of the foregoing.

"HS/1 Reserved Materials" means the copyrighted expression and non-public
implementation materials relating to SEAM-HS/1 Holographic Surfaces, including:

- the HS/1 specification, explanatory text, diagrams, examples, container
  format, headers, metadata, authored arrangements, and visual designs;
- source code and documentation for surface compilation, pixel packing,
  encoding, decoding, hashing, verification, repair, storage, lookup, query,
  context extraction, import, export, rendering, and provenance;
- surface libraries, adapters, SDK, CLI, API, MCP, dashboard, benchmark, test,
  fixture, and integration material that implements, exposes, evaluates, or is
  derived from the non-public HS/1 implementation; and
- non-public modifications, extensions, ports, translations, or derivative
  works of any of the foregoing.

"Authorized Contributor" means a person whom the Project Owner has expressly
authorized in writing to access the Private Repository for work on SEAM.

"Legacy Apache Materials" means only the exact file versions that the Project
Owner previously published in the public repository at
https://github.com/BlackhatShiftey/Seam_Runtime while those versions carried
the Apache License, Version 2.0. The public repository's commit history
identifies those versions.

